    // fdid -> [game types], or all game types if empty
    // completely skip processing the given model
    // (use this if the system claims the model is similar to a blacklist, but it is not, either to
    // shut up the "beware these animations are similar" spam, or to resolve false positives)
    // BEWARE: usually, it is better to add an empty blacklist than a whitelist, since the blacklist
    // system will propagate the empty playlist to other models that are similar, but this is an
    // easier way of eliminating noise without that side effect
